 / `--workspace doctor`, or positional arguments to other subcommands such as `nexus trust check`), any non-doctor invocation containing `\"doctor\"` or `\"check\"` as an argument value bypasses the startup exit at line 99.\n   - Furthermore, several CLI subcommands and pre-config startup actions do **not** call `buildConfig()`:\n     - `nexus -w check skills` (exits `0` and runs the `skills` command despite `~/.config/nexus/config.json` containing `{broken`).\n     - `nexus trust check` / `nexus trust doctor` (mutates trusted workspace state without calling `buildConfig()`).\n     - `nexus gc`, `nexus sessions`, `nexus mcp -w check`, `nexus plugins -w check`.\n     - In `runDefault()` (`nexus --live -w check`), `promptWorkspaceTrust()`, `triggerBackgroundGc()`, and `spawnTui()` execute before `buildConfig()`.\n     - At `cli/src/index.ts:106`, `recoverUpgrade(process.env.NEXUS_HOME)` runs before `program.parseAsync(process.argv)` whenever line 99 does not exit.\n\n2. **Reproduction (Verified in Isolated Worktree \u0026 `$HOME`)**:\n   ```bash\n   HOME_TMP=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\n   mkdir -p \"$HOME_TMP/.config/nexus\"\n   printf '{broken\\n' \u003e \"$HOME_TMP/.config/nexus/config.json\"\n   HOME=\"$HOME_TMP\" node --import tsx cli/src/index.ts -w check skills\n   # Actual: exits 0 (\"No skills found...\") instead of exiting 2 with Configuration error\n   ```\n\n3. **Required Fix**:\n   - Do not match arbitrary argument positions with `startupArgs.some((arg) =\u003e arg === \"doctor\" || arg === \"check\")`.\n   - Restrict the pre-parse exemption to when the top-level subcommand token itself is `doctor` or `check` (e.g., `startupArgs[0] === \"doctor\" || startupArgs[0] === \"check\"`), **and** register a Commander `program.hook(\"preAction\", (_thisCommand, actionCommand) =\u003e ...)` guard so that any resolved command other than `doctor` / `check` immediately exits `2` if `operatorConfigLoadError()` is non-null.\n   - Add a regression test in `cli/test/operator_config_startup.test.ts` verifying that a non-doctor command with `\"check\"` or `\"doctor\"` in its arguments (e.g., `[\"-w\", \"check\", \"skills\"]` or `[\"trust\", \"check\"]`) still fails closed with exit code `2` when `~/.config/nexus/config.json` is malformed.","createdAt":"2026-10-28T07:32:08Z","url":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299#issuecomment-6463342276"}
