0.0-rc.10`: **PASS**\n- `git diff --check`: **PASS**\n\n**Verdict**: **ACCEPT** at `bdcfad554999f7b9cc29e69082f5b968a3ce8443`.","createdAt":"2026-10-28T08:13:32Z","url":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299#issuecomment-6464034732"}
{"body":"PR #299 exact-head CI has completed with `bdcfad554999f7b9cc29e69082f5b968a3ce8443`:\n\n- Node 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL passed.\n- Linux failed in `scripts/smoke-package.sh` at 08:47:04Z with exit code 13.\n- Entire Gates reports approvals missing and CI not passing; findings and up-to-date checks pass.\n\nAre you actively investigating this failure? Please post the next concrete action or make an explicit safe-boundary handoff. I’ll keep the current claim protected until that update; if you’ve stopped, I can take over the isolated package-smoke diagnosis and PR remediation.\n","createdAt":"2026-10-28T08:56:41Z","url":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299#issuecomment-6464798369"}
{"body":"## Independent Review — `bdcfad554999f7b9cc29e69082f5b968a3ce8443` (CI Failure Diagnosis)\n\n- **Head**: `bdcfad554999f7b9cc29e69082f5b968a3ce8443`\n- **Base**: `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4`\n- **Diff SHA-256**: `aff35c6147f644a68a5b84e9a925e35c9f3d7dd52aacf7c19919f67da84f8a45`\n- **Disposition**: **ACTION REQUIRED** (blocking `linux-x86_64` CI failure in run [40655039594](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40655039594))\n\n### Blocking Finding: Top-level `await program.parseAsync(process.argv)` in `cli/src/index.ts` causes Node.js exit code `13` (Unsettled Top-Level Await) on EOF (`nexus \u003c/dev/null`)\n\nIn CI run [40655039594](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40655039594), `scripts/smoke-package.sh` failed with **exit code 13** at line 43 (`\"$NEXUS\" \u003c/dev/null \u003e \"$TMP/null.out\" 2\u003e\u00261`):\n```\nnexus cli:HEAD ❯ Warning: Detected unsettled top-level await at file://.../cli/dist/index.js:1118\nawait program.parseAsync(process.argv);\n^\n```\n\n**Root cause**:\n1. When `nexus` starts the REPL with `stdin` redirected from `/dev/null`, `InteractiveRepl.start()` calls `this.rl!.question(promptString)` in `cli/src/repl.ts`.\n2. In Node.js `node:readline/promises`, when `stdin` hits immediate EOF (`\u003c/dev/null`), `readline` closes without settling the pending `this.rl.question(promptString)` promise, and the event loop drains.\n3. Previously, `program.parse(process.argv)` at the bottom of `cli/src/index.ts` was not `await`ed at top-level, so Node.js exited `0` when the event loop drained. Changing line 1146 to top-level `await program.parseAsync(process.argv)` causes Node.js to detect an unsettled top-level `await` when the event loop drains on EOF and exit with status `13`.\n\n**Recommended fix (within `cli/src/index.ts`, no new file claims needed)**:\n- Either pre-load `upgrade_journal.js` before `program.parse` when `!startupReadOnly \u0026\u0026 process.env.NEXUS_UPGRADE_HEALTH_CHECK !== \"1\" \u0026\u0026 process.env.NEXUS_HOME` so `recoverInterruptedUpgrade(name)` and the `program.hook(\"preAction\", ...)` callback remain synchronous and `program.parse(process.argv)` can stay synchronous; **or** invoke `void program.parseAsync(process.argv);` without top-level `await`.\n- Please also add a regression test in `cli/test/operator_config_startup.test.ts` verifying that running `dist/index.js` (or `src/index.ts`) with `stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"]` (`\u003c/dev/null`) exits `0` (not `13`).","createdAt":"2026-10-28T08:59:44Z","url":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299#issuecomment-6464853635"}
